# [DD-13b.W23.3a] THE SAME RESOLVED REAL PATH, REACHED BY TWO SPELLINGS,
# IN ONE FILE'S OWN `include` LINES — §2.5's collision rule, the one
# slice of it a SINGLE file's own parse can decide without walking
# anything else (`src/parse/rxt_source.c`'s duplicate-target loop, added
# alongside the row itself). `"include_basic_frag.rxtfrag"` and
# `"./include_basic_frag.rxtfrag"` are two different STRINGS that
# `realpath(3)` resolves to the same file.
#
# `check_refusal` — SINGLE-LEG, leg A only — exactly `dup_head_
# description.rxtin`'s own wording pattern and for the identical reason:
# this file is head-bearing (`include` is a head declaration), the head
# has one parser by the seam ruling (`w1_impl.md` §1.1), and a three-leg
# assertion on a head-level refusal is not available at any point in
# this format's life. Naming BOTH lines is the assertion: a refusal
# naming one is a RED, because a collision has two ends.
include "include_basic_frag.rxtfrag"
include "./include_basic_frag.rxtfrag"

pattern top
m "top" 0 3
